{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired node1’s status writer. SIGHUP now reloads valid configuration in-place, empty configuration is rejected while retaining the last valid message, SIGTERM exits cleanly, exactly one writer runs, journal history is preserved, and the service recovered automatically after a verified node reboot.","actions_performed":["Reimplemented worker.py using dependency-free POSIX shell compatible with the installed Alpine platform.","Added and enabled an OpenRC status-writer service.","Verified valid SIGHUP reload with unchanged PID and one writer.","Verified whitespace-only and zero-byte configurations are rejected.","Verified clean SIGTERM exit status 0.","Restored message.conf to `branch status: open`.","Restarted node1 safely and verified boot identity changed and all required state recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SIGHUP reloads message.conf without terminating the process or creating a second writer","command_ids":["cmd-28c3e14b39184737"],"summary":"PID remained 3185, writer count remained one, and subsequent entries changed to `branch status: reloaded`."},{"requirement":"Reject empty configuration while retaining the last valid message","command_ids":["cmd-836971f0de094710"],"summary":"A zero-byte configuration was rejected; PID stayed 2319 and the writer continued appending `branch status: open`. The valid configuration was restored."},{"requirement":"Exit cleanly on SIGTERM","command_ids":["cmd-8d6b0e02e77a4d4a","cmd-c8d672037b4d4d68"],"summary":"OpenRC stopped the writer with no remaining process; a direct TERM test returned wait exit status 0."},{"requirement":"Continue appending and preserve existing journal entries","command_ids":["cmd-1330a3f3a0774c95","cmd-4c7e55866f3e48cc","cmd-836971f0de094710"],"summary":"The original first entry `branch status: opening` remains present, while line counts increased and current messages continued appending."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and